From 934549a84cbb48a29bac8dce246a8946f2fb52d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aamir <aamir@tallow-lang.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:19:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] codegen+runtime+interp: bind Crawler.from_sitemap, and
 stop the crawler arms coercing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The last unbound native now has all three legs, so the declared `// native` surface is fully
bound and that claim is checkable by grep rather than by trusting a plan note. Like the
StructuredData binding, this adds no capability: the interpreter already fetched through
`SitemapParser` over `runtime::egress_http` (Tor by default, refusing rather than falling
back to the box IP). What it removes is the asymmetry where the compiled path silently fell
back to the interpreter, and refused outright under --require-native.

The FFI returns the discovered `seed_url` and writes the echoed `sitemap_url`, the constant
`strategy` and the four integers through out-params — the `tallow_crawler_from_links`
convention, including reading every field BY NAME so a reordered field refuses rather than
shifting silently.

Both crawler arms also stopped coercing their argument. They used `v.as_string()`, so
`Crawler.from_links(42)` planned a crawler for the seed "42" and `Crawler.from_sitemap(42)`
would have attempted discovery on it. That is the same defect class the structured-data
refusal test exposed, in the same file, and it is fixed the same way: match `Value::String`,
refuse anything else, and share the wording with the compiled arm so the two engines name
the same cause.

Scope, stated rather than implied: `Crawler.from_links` plans offline (`crawler_from_links_plan`
is pure), so it gets the full three-assertion parity treatment with a pinned reference.
`Crawler.from_sitemap` FETCHES, so its happy path cannot be exercised offline — a local fixture
can never be fetched, which the facade's own doc records. What is deterministic offline is the
refusal, rejected before any egress, and that is what the tests pin.

Verified: cargo check --lib --bins; crawler_parity 3/0; structured_data_parity 2/0;
the runtime FFI suite; the codegen suite.
